# Recipe: content with no source file of its own.  The name "font/cascadiamono/16" is this
# file's path under content/ minus the extension; "kind" is what it cooks to, which decides
# the cooked file name (font -> font/cascadiamono/16.orb_font).  The remaining lines are the
# bake inputs: face is a font_tool input (a TTF under assets/font_source or an OS-installed
# face name), size is the pixel size; optional "sdf <spread>" bakes a distance field and
# optional "range <spec>" bakes past ASCII (see font_tool -range).

kind    font
face    CascadiaMono
size    16
